9M2PJU HamClock Installer (Open HamClock / OHB Edition)
Backend: https://ohb.hamclock.app

HamClock is a kiosk-style application that provides real time space weather, radio propagation models,
operating events, satellite tracking, and other information particularly useful to the radio amateur.

For comprehensive documentation, build instructions, and one-liner installer scripts, see README.md.

Executive summary for UNIX / Linux / Raspberry Pi / macOS / FreeBSD systems:
    Run the universal installer:
        ./install.sh
    Or manual build:
        make <target>   (e.g., make hamclock-800x480 or make hamclock-1600x960)
        sudo make install

Executive summary for ESP8266:
    install and run Arduino IDE
    open ESPHamClock.ino in IDE
    Sketch -> Compile
    Sketch -> Upload
